canonical_claim.statement:
[Printed] The chain of item 2 on p. 1517, as transcribed in P005-T3.
[Sol's corrected text (validated.json, P005-E002, smallest_repair), verbatim, second part] “On p. 1517 apply this with $a^c=h-d$ and $b^c=y(1)-\overline{y(1)}$. The same standing assumptions imply $|h_i-d|\le n\kappa$, $n^{-1}\sum_i(h_i-d)^2\le n\kappa d$, and $n^{-1}\sum_i(y_i(1)-\overline{y(1)})^2\le K$. Thus the unscaled variance remains $O(n\kappa^2+\kappa d/n)$ and the scaled variance remains $O(\kappa^2/n+\kappa d/n^3)$.”
[Corrected chain, with every hypothesis] Fix $n \ge 4$ and $1 \le n_T \le n-1$, under complete randomization. Suppose $\bar x = 0$ and $\overline{xx'} = I_d$ (Assumption 2 at this $n$) and $\frac1n\sum_iy_i(1)^2 \le K$ (Assumption 1); $h_i = \|x_i\|_2^2$ and $\kappa = \max_ih_i/n$. Write $u_i = h_i - d$ and $v_i = y_i(1) - \overline{y(1)}$. Then
(a) $\bar h = d$, $0 \le h_i \le n\kappa$ and $d \le n\kappa$, so $|u_i| \le n\kappa$;
(b) $\frac1n\sum_iu_i^2 = \frac1n\sum_ih_i^2 - d^2 \le \frac1n\sum_ih_i^2 \le n\kappa d$;
(c) $\frac1n\sum_iv_i^2 = \frac1n\sum_iy_i(1)^2 - \overline{y(1)}^2 \le K$;
(d) $\frac1n\sum_i(u_iv_i - \overline{uv})^2 \le \frac1n\sum_iu_i^2v_i^2 \le n^2\kappa^2K$;
(e) $$\mathrm{Var}\big[\overline{hy(1)}_T - \bar h_T\overline{y(1)}_T\big] \le \frac{2(n-n_T)}{n_T(n-1)}\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^n\big(u_iv_i - \overline{uv}\big)^2 + \frac{2(n-n_T)n}{n_T^3(n-1)}\Big(\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^nu_i^2\Big)\Big(\frac1n\sum_{i=1}^nv_i^2\Big) \le \frac{2(n-n_T)}{n_T(n-1)}n^2\kappa^2K + \frac{2(n-n_T)n}{n_T^3(n-1)}n\kappa dK.$$
(f) [Order statement, as printed] Along a sequence of populations satisfying Assumptions 1–3, the right-hand side of (e) is $O\big(\kappa^2n + \frac{\kappa d}{n}\big)$, and therefore $\mathrm{Var}\big(\frac1n(\overline{hy(1)}_T - \bar h_T\overline{y(1)}_T)\big) = O\big(\frac{\kappa^2}{n} + \frac{\kappa d}{n^3}\big)$. Explicitly, if $p_{\min} < n_T/n$ then $\frac{2(n-n_T)}{n_T(n-1)} \le \frac{2}{p_{\min}(n-1)}$ and $\frac{2(n-n_T)n}{n_T^3(n-1)} \le \frac{2}{p_{\min}^3n(n-1)}$.
The same statements hold for the control arm, with $y(0)$, $n_C$ and $\widehat{\mathrm{Cov}}_C$ in place of $y(1)$, $n_T$ and $\widehat{\mathrm{Cov}}_T$ (and $1 - p_{\max}$ in place of $p_{\min}$).
